# Playable level prototype (M4-B, PR-43): .plt ground parser, extended
# .MOV grammar (F=/T=/G= physics, TARGET(p)=COND transitions) and the
# player runtime. The selftest is hermetic (synthetic .plt + real walk
# CONSTANTS), so it runs in EVERY configuration; the scripted demo legs
# run on the real RAN.01 / TUNGA.11 player data (LEW.* leaves).
verify-play: ll_level
# PR-97 RE-PIN NOTE (applies to every y in this target): the player's x,y
# is the POSITION POINT; what stands on the .plt line is the animation's
# shape-box bottom (ll_seq_shape_contact -> ll_player.contact, and the same
# rule for ground-bound placements through obj_settle/obj_contact). So every
# grounded position point moved UP by exactly that art set's offset, which
# is a property of the art, not a constant:
#   RAN.01 LEW.RAN/UJ09.SEQ: 10..14 px per frame, 14 as the animation value
#     (its 59-row art hangs 45 rows above the point and 10-14 below it, the
#     lifted-paw frames less) -> the 298/313 values become 286/299;
#   ZARIA.01 LEW.ZAR: WALK 32, TURN 29, FIGHT 34, IDLE 28 px -> the 680
#     floor becomes 648 while walking (that art is centred on the point).
# The offset is taken once per ANIMATION (the max over the state's frame
# list, ll_level.c mov_state_contact) and a state change while grounded
# keeps the CONTACT LINE invariant (play_advance): what never moves is the
# surface, so the logged position point differs between states that carry a
# different shape bottom (648 walking, 652 idling on the same grass line) and
# never depends on which frame or which state came before. Scene-object
# placements move the same way.
# data-free leg: parser + physics + transition selftest (always runs)
	@timeout 30 ./ll_level --play-selftest
# data-free leg (PR-137): the viewer's OWN camera law - the PR-136
# grounded anchor and the clamp that fakes it at the ground line, the
# spawn snap, the invented eases, the airborne hold, both leads, the
# world-edge clamps. Every value hand-derived; no game data.
	@timeout 30 ./ll_level --follow-selftest
# data-free leg (PR-531): the life chain - below the line writes ONLY
# energy -1 (0x54478), the next step spends exactly one life through
# the consumer (0x503fb-0x5042b stand-in), the zero arms loop code 2
# and not before (0x4ae82-0x4ae8b), and the code-2 consumer resets the
# counter to 5 (0x5d2f9) and stops through its empty-queue leg
# (0x5d38e). Synthetic script, no game data.
	@timeout 30 ./ll_level --lives-selftest
# data-free leg (PR-533): the death LINE - the main_back layer's
# height + 0x1f4 (0x54452-0x5446e), the back_rect-height fallback on
# a NULL desc (0x572f5), the movsx word read (0x54467). RED-FIRST:
# this leg FAILS while death_line still returns the authored rects;
# it is the assertion the flip of the law must turn green.
	@timeout 30 ./ll_level --line-selftest
ifeq ($(PX_DATA),1)
# PR-135 RE-PIN NOTE (applies to every "play tick N" and every
# LEO_PLAY_SCRIPT / LEO_LEVEL_PPM_TICK value in this target): LEO_LEVEL_PPM
# now runs ONE engine iteration per tick (LL_ITER_MS = 50 ms), so a tick
# index IS an iteration index and the m-th feed of any row list is exactly
# entry+m-1 - the ceil(28m/20) offsets PR-110 had to carry are gone, and
# every script index below is the old one times 2/5 (the same wall clock in
# seconds), every position is the law's, and every row boundary is a whole
# number of ticks. The legs that keep a tick index unchanged are the ones
# whose pin does not depend on elapsed time (the p2 turn leg).
# PR-231 RE-PIN NOTE (applies to every ZARIA.01 ground position in this
# target): the engine's control parser maps CHECK_ALL to 0x1c0 and so
# implies the CHECK_LN keep-ground rule (read PR-230, OI-113), and every
# ZARIA.01 lion state carries CHECK_ALL. ZARIA.01's A_WALK now follows
# the authored first polyline `-50,680!408,684` (ZARIA_A.PLT): a grounded
# y there is line(x)-contact, so the pre-PR-231 flat 648 becomes 649 for
# x past ~-40 (line 681) and 650/651/652 further right; jumps launched
# there lift off from the sloped line (apex y +1); the walk ENDS at the
# polyline's end x=408 (the traverse leg says so in full). The numbers
# are the re-pinned law's own arithmetic on the authored bytes, not
# fitted. RAN.01 legs do not shift: RAN spells CHECK_LN explicitly and
# already followed its ground.
# PR-523 RE-PIN NOTE (applies to every position and every row timing in
# this target): the port now runs the intent word at the full scale 20
# (PR-522's cold-start seed evidence) and a physics PASS runs at a ROW
# ADMIT - plus the intent edge and the zero-FEED-WORD restart, one
# seed pass each (ported/ll_play.c; PR-529 re-keys PR-523's
# register-zero arm onto [obj+0xca] - a zero register leaves a zero
# word, so the reversal case below is unchanged). A walk's add is idiv(F*s,20) plus the
# authored G_x word on the admit path (PR-521), the drag idiv(v*T,100):
# RAN.01's [A_WALK] settles the register at 445 = the fixed point of a
# 400 add against a 90% drag, and ZARIA.01's [A_WALK] (its authored
# G=30,350 rides the add: 100+30 = 130 a pass) settles at 650. The
# body steps idiv(v,100) whole px PER PASS and the BY_X feed is that
# step, so the authored 6-unit rows close two admits per three ticks at
# full intent and the walk runs ABOVE PR-134's measured [38,76] u/s -
# the live capture's per-iteration register stepping is why, and the
# same named item owns it (OI-013). Every tick, position and frame
# index below is re-derived from that arithmetic (the mirrors in the
# PR-523 record reproduce the port leg for leg); the object-side
# creatures keep the PR-79/134 measured pitch - ll_level.c's obj_walk
# spells its scale 10.0 and does NOT follow the lion's constant.
# scripted demo on REAL player data: walk right (FWD), reverse (BKWD),
